odot/issues/98947#issuecomment-2495312819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98947","id":2495312819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Uu3Oz","user":{"login":"AshbyGeek","id":83048,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMDQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83048?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek","html_url":"https://github.com/AshbyGeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AshbyGeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-23T04:53:06Z","updated_at":"2024-11-23T05:20:28Z","body":"Can confirm this, from a project of my own. ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c778df6-0336-45eb-a1ca-431322ee4b35) running godot 4.4.dev4.mono\n\nHonestly, it looks like the same problem but the fix assumed the problem only happened when the camera is inside the fog volume. In PR #86103, fog.cpp line 694 what happens if you change the condition to:\n\n```\nif (cam_position.x > (corner_min.x - expand) && cam_position.x < (corner_max.x + expand) ||\n\tcam_position.y > (corner_min.y - expand) && cam_position.y < (corner_max.y + expand) ||\n\tcam_position.z > (corner_min.z - expand) && cam_position.z < (corner_max.z + expand))\n```\n\nWhen I get a chance I'll try compiling godot myself and make the change, but I haven't set up to compile it yet and don't know how long that will take me.